language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ crossword: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ Complete the crossword puzzle below (# is a blocked square; the numbers 1 to 8 mark the squares where words start):
$
$        1   2   3   4   5
$      +---+---+---+---+---+
$    1 | 1 |   | 2 |   | 3 |
$    2 | # | # |   | # |   |
$    3 | # | 4 |   | 5 |   |
$    4 | 6 | # | 7 |   |   |
$    5 | 8 |   |   |   |   |
$    6 |   | # | # |   | # |
$      +---+---+---+---+---+
$
$ Words: AFT, ALE, EEL, HEEL, HIKE, HOSES, KEEL, KNOT, LASER, LEE, LINE, SAILS, SHEET, STEER, TIE.
$ Select 8 of these 15 words, each used once, so that the puzzle can be completed with them.
$
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/crossword.html
$ Save this model as model.eprime and run it with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the solution is
$ written to `model.eprime.solution`:
$   savilerow model.eprime -run-solver

$ Words[w,k]: the k-th letter (A=1 ... Z=26) of word w+1, padded with 0; word w is numbered from 0 in the order longest first, then alphabetically (HOSES is 0, TIE is 14)
letting Words be [[8,15,19,5,19],[12,1,19,5,18],[19,1,9,12,19],[19,8,5,5,20],[19,20,5,5,18],[8,5,5,12,0],[8,9,11,5,0],[11,5,5,12,0],[11,14,15,20,0],[12,9,14,5,0],[1,6,20,0,0],[1,12,5,0,0],[5,5,12,0,0],[12,5,5,0,0],[20,9,5,0,0]]
$ Len[w+1]: the number of letters of word w (same numbering as Words)
letting Len be [5,5,5,5,5,4,4,4,4,4,3,3,3,3,3]
$ RunLen[n]: the number of squares of the run that starts at numbered square n
letting RunLen be [5,5,5,4,4,3,3,5]
$ Open[r,c]: the square in row r, column c is open (not blocked)
letting Open be [[true,true,true,true,true],[false,false,true,false,true],[false,true,true,true,true],[true,false,true,true,true],[true,true,true,true,true],[true,false,false,true,false]]

$ E[n]: the word (numbered from 0 as above) that starts at numbered square n
find E : matrix indexed by [int(1..8)] of int(0..14)
$ auxiliary: the letter in each square of the grid (0 for a blocked square)
find L : matrix indexed by [int(1..6), int(1..5)] of int(0..26)

such that
$ the eight chosen words are all different
allDiff(E),
$ each numbered run has the length of its chosen word, for each of the eight runs
forAll n : int(1..8) . Len[E[n]+1] = RunLen[n],
$ the squares of the grid are open exactly where they should be: open squares hold a letter, blocked squares hold 0
forAll r : int(1..6) . forAll c : int(1..5) . (Open[r,c] -> L[r,c] > 0) /\ (!Open[r,c] -> L[r,c] = 0),
$ across square 1 (row 1) spells its word
forAll k : int(1..5) . L[1,k] = Words[E[1]+1,k],
$ down square 2 (column 3, rows 1 to 5) spells its word
forAll k : int(1..5) . L[k,3] = Words[E[2]+1,k],
$ down square 3 (column 5, rows 1 to 5) spells its word
forAll k : int(1..5) . L[k,5] = Words[E[3]+1,k],
$ across square 4 (row 3, columns 2 to 5) spells its word
forAll k : int(1..4) . L[3,k+1] = Words[E[4]+1,k],
$ down square 5 (column 4, rows 3 to 6) spells its word
forAll k : int(1..4) . L[k+2,4] = Words[E[5]+1,k],
$ down square 6 (column 1, rows 4 to 6) spells its word
forAll k : int(1..3) . L[k+3,1] = Words[E[6]+1,k],
$ across square 7 (row 4, columns 3 to 5) spells its word
forAll k : int(1..3) . L[4,k+2] = Words[E[7]+1,k],
$ across square 8 (row 5, columns 1 to 5) spells its word
forAll k : int(1..5) . L[5,k] = Words[E[8]+1,k]
